<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore bunkers steady, 180-cst at $130-$132/T.</title>
<headline>Singapore bunkers steady, 180-cst at $130-$132/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore bunkers were quoted little changed from Monday but overnight crude gains and demand may push prices higher later Tuesday, traders said.</p>
<p>Bunker 180-cst prices were quoted at $130-$132 for both majors and independents and 380-cst indications were seen at $126-$128 per tonne.</p>
<p>Traders said enquiries were thin but expected more demand later today. But some sellers were mixed on near term market direction, citing a very quiet cargo market.</p>
<p>MDO and gas oil quotes were steady at $230-$250 and $254-$257 respectively. --Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3082)</p>
</text>
